{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AVvtBeuJpztQ9Cyx1iA1T4","type":"tool_result","content":";; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n---README\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final answer the graders\n  read (from `final.txt` for Codex, from the event stream for Kimi).\n\nLanes:\n\n- `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.\n- `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the\n  macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real\n  home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in\n  `~/.kimi-code`, which the profile opens.\n\nCodex logs in with an API key from the environment (`CODEX_API_KEY`), so it\nneeds nothing from the home folder.\n---check\n\"\"\"The final answer of a run, as the graders read it: final.txt (Codex lanes), else the last assistant message in\nthe Kimi stream-json log. usage: check_answer.py <run folder>  ->  {\"final\": \"...\", \"source\": \"...\"}\"\"\"\nimport json, os, sys\n\nR = sys.argv[1]\ndef read(p):\n    try: return open(p, errors=\"replace\").read()\n    except OSError: return \"\"\n\nfinal, source = read(os.path.join(R, \"final.txt\")), \"final.txt\"\nlane = json.loads(read(os.path.join(R, \"meta.json\")) or \"{}\").get(\"lane\", \"\")\nif not final.strip() and lane.startswith(\"kimi\"):\n    source = \"agent.log\"\n    for line in reversed(read(os.path.join(R, \"agent.log\")).splitlines()):\n        try: d = json.loads(line)\n        except ValueError: continue\n        if d.get(\"role\") == \"assistant\" and isinstance(d.get(\"content\"), str) and d[\"content\"].strip():\n            final = d[\"content\"]; break\nprint(json.dumps({\"final\": final, \"source\": source if final.strip() else \"none\"}))\n---gitignore\nruns/*\n!runs/.keep\n---prompt\nfizz.py prints the wrong word for multiples of 15. Fix it and say what was wrong.\n---fizz\ndef fizz(n):\n    if n % 3 == 0:\n        return \"Fizz\"\n    if n % 5 == 0:\n        return \"Buzz\"\n    if n % 15 == 0:\n        return \"FizzBuzz\"\n    return str(n)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    print(\" \".join(fizz(i) for i in range(1, 16)))\n\ntotal 16\ndrwx------  10 valentinakoniukhova wheel   320 Nov  9 14:50 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 591 root                wheel 18912 Nov  9 14:51 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x  12 valentinakoniukhova wheel   384 Nov  9 14:51 .git\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel    19 Nov  9 14:50 .gitignore\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1174 Nov  9 14:50 README.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel   938 Nov  9 14:50 check_answer.py\n-rwxr-xr-x   1 valentinakoniukhova wheel  1601 Nov  9 14:50 run.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 14:50 runs\ndrwxr-xr-x   3 valentinakoniukhova wheel    96 Nov  9 14:50 sandbox\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 valentinakoniukhova wheel   128 Nov  9 14:50 tasks\n/opt/homebrew/bin/codex\n/usr/bin/sandbox-exec\ntotal 185156\ndrwxr-xr-x  5 valentinakoniukhova staff       160 Nov  7 00:24 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 21 valentinakoniukhova staff       672 Nov  9 03:42 ..\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova staff   2953808 Mar 10  2026 fd\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova staff 182590912 Nov  6 23:51 kimi\n-rwxr-xr-x  1 valentinakoniukhova staff   4048800 Nov  7 00:24 rg","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"de1a175d-3615-41f9-8a54-3e9cd380a86a","uuid":"348a4621-1a79-4ab1-bce0-d7d075d62b3e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T17:51:03.817Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":";; OS-level fence for lanes whose output leaves the machine: the agent has a real shell, so the real home must be\n;; unreachable. Only the agent's own install is opened. Network stays open. HOME is passed with -D HOME=<real home>.\n(version 1)\n(allow default)\n(deny file-read-data (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(deny file-write* (subpath (param \"HOME\")))\n(allow file-read-data (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(allow file-write* (subpath (string-append (param \"HOME\") \"/.kimi-code\")))\n(deny process-exec (literal \"/bin/launchctl\") (literal \"/usr/bin/security\") (literal \"/usr/bin/osascript\"))\n---README\n# agent-evals\n\nA small harness that runs coding agents on short tasks and keeps everything a\nrun produced, so the runs can be graded and compared later. It lives in\n`~/evals/agent-evals` on the eval Mac.\n\n`./run.sh <task> <lane> [rep]` copies `tasks/<task>/` into a scratch folder in\n`/tmp`, runs the lane's agent there with `tasks/<task>.prompt`, and writes the\nrun folder `runs/<task>-<lane>-r<rep>/`:\n\n- `prompt.txt`, `agent.log` (the agent's JSON event stream), `agent.err`,\n  `meta.json` (exit code, seconds);\n- `final.txt`, the agent's last message, for the Codex lanes;\n- `answer.json`, written by `check_answer.py`: the final ans